{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issues_index.json\\\")); print(type(d).__name__); print(json.dumps([x for x in (d if isinstance(d,list) else d.get(\\\"issues\\\", [])) if x.get(\\\"number\\\") in [2015,1022,1076,2158,3207]], indent=2))'\"","aggregated_output":"list\n[\n  {\n    \"number\": 1022,\n    \"title\": \"Progress on generator\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2021-02-17T12:46:51Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": \"2021-02-17T16:57:29Z\",\n    \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n    \"body\": \"Hi @willmcgugan ,\\r\\n\\r\\nI hope to find you well. Thank you for this amazing library. I was wondering how can I use the `progress.track` function to track a generator since `total` is required but generators have no length.\\r\\n\\r\\nThank you.\\r\\n\\r\\nCheers,\\r\\n\\r\\nFrancesco\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"number\": 1076,\n    \"title\": \"Double Live Tables?\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2021-02-28T19:18:02Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": \"2021-02-28T19:27:53Z\",\n    \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n    \"body\": \"Trying to print out two live tables with different headers/column count. Apparently can't stack double live tables.\\r\\n```\\r\\n    with Live(generate_table(), refresh_per_second=4) as live:\\r\\n        with Live(generate_table2(), refresh_per_second=4) as live2:\\r\\n            while True:\\r\\n                sleep(0.4)\\r\\n                live.update(generate_table())\\r\\n                live2.update(generate_table2())\\r\\n```\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\\"Only one live display may be active at once\\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\nWhat is the workaround?\\r\\nThank you!\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"number\": 2015,\n    \"title\": \"Thank you note!\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2022-03-02T12:29:36Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": \"2022-03-02T21:28:00Z\",\n    \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n    \"body\": \"This is waaaaay too cool thank you! \\r\\n\\r\\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/9364931/156361507-ef070a94-d21a-43a9-81bb-c8ad27ee7d48.png)\\r\\n\\r\\n(I'm working on a Pelican plugin and Pelican uses Rich to format the stacktraces)\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"number\": 2158,\n    \"title\": \"Rich Live display not updating the terminal \",\n    \"created_at\": \"2022-04-04T10:37:11Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": \"2022-04-04T12:56:30Z\",\n    \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n    \"body\": \"Hi, I hope everyone is ok, I am trying to display multiple progress bars with Rich. My program uses python concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor to run multiple tasks at the same time. I am using a table to display the progress bars, the table and progress bars are displayed correctly in the terminal, but all progress bars remain at zero until the end.\\r\\n\\r\\n```python\\r\\nimport concurrent.futures\\r\\n\\r\\ntask_progress = Progress(\\r\\n    \\\"{task.description}\\\",\\r\\n    SpinnerColumn(),\\r\\n    BarColumn(),\\r\\n    TextColumn(\\\"[progress.percentage]{task.percentage:>3.0f}%\\\"),\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef process_chunk(\\r\\n    chunk: list[tuple, None, None],\\r\\n    comparison_indexes: list[int],\\r\\n    rows: list[tuple[str]],\\r\\n    rate: int,\\r\\n    task_id: TaskID,\\r\\n) -> list[list[tuple[str]]]:\\r\\n    for row in chunk:\\r\\n    ...\\r\\n        for task in task_progress.tasks:\\r\\n            task_progress.advance(task_id)\\r\\n            if not task.finished:\\r\\n                task_progress.advance(task_id)\\r\\n           # task_progress.advance(task_id)\\r\\n    return groups\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef main():\\r\\n    ...\\r\\n    chunks = [...] # a list of Iterable\\r\\n    ...\\r\\n    tasks_ids = [\\r\\n        task_progress.add_task(description=\\\"Processing...\\\", total=len(chunk))\\r\\n        for chunk in chunks\\r\\n    ]\\r\\n    progress_table = Table.grid()\\r\\n    progress_table.add_row(\\r\\n        Panel.fit(task_progress, title=\\\"[b]Jobs\\\", border_style=\\\"red\\\", padding=(1, 2))\\r\\n    )\\r\\n    ...\\r\\n     with Live(progress_table, refresh_per_second=10):\\r\\n        with concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor() as executor:\\r\\n            groups = executor.map(\\r\\n                process_chunk,\\r\\n                chunks,\\r\\n                tuple(itertools.repeat(comparison_indexes, chunks_len)),\\r\\n                tuple(itertools.repeat(rows, chunks_len)),\\r\\n                tuple(itertools.repeat(args.rate, chunks_len)),\\r\\n                tasks_ids,\\r\\n            )\\r\\n```\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"number\": 3207,\n    \"title\": \"[BUG]When there are too many progress bars, all progress bars cannot be displayed\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2023-11-18T06:48:10Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"state_reason\": null,\n    \"body\": \"- [x] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions.\\r\\n- [x] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md).\\r\\n\\r\\n**Describe the bug**\\r\\n\\r\\nMy program needs to display multiple progress bars. When the progress bar fills the entire screen, the remaining progress bars will not be displayed until all progress bars are completed.\\r\\n\\r\\n![1700288051394](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/assets/49263334/9ee6965e-d94f-44db-bbdf-6f5932c1ee3e)\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nfrom rich.console import Console\\r\\nfrom rich.progress import (\\r\\n    Progress,\\r\\n    TextColumn,\\r\\n    BarColumn,\\r\\n    DownloadColumn,\\r\\n    TimeRemainingColumn,\\r\\n)\\r\\nimport time\\r\\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\\r\\n\\r\\nconsole = Console()\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef progress_object():\\r\\n    return Progress(\\r\\n        TextColumn(\\r\\n            \\\"[progress.description]{task.description}\\\",\\r\\n            justify=\\\"left\\\"),\\r\\n        \\\"\\u2022\\\",\\r\\n        BarColumn(\\r\\n            bar_width=20),\\r\\n        \\\"[progress.percentage]{task.percentage:>3.1f}%\\\",\\r\\n        \\\"\\u2022\\\",\\r\\n        DownloadColumn(\\r\\n            binary_units=True),\\r\\n        \\\"\\u2022\\\",\\r\\n        TimeRemainingColumn(),\\r\\n        console=console,\\r\\n    expand=True\\r\\n    )\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef download(progress, i):\\r\\n    task_id = progress.add_task(\\r\\n        f\\\"task {i}\\\", total=10)\\r\\n    for _ in range(10):\\r\\n        time.sleep(0.2)\\r\\n        progress.update(task_id, advance=1)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nwith progress_object() as progress:\\r\\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as pool:\\r\\n        for i in range(100):\\r\\n            pool.submit(download, progress, i)\\r\\n\\r\\n```\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
